  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n4x - 3y = 12 and xy = 5\n\n**Concept used:**\n\n(a - b)2 = a2 + b2 - 2ab\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n4x - 3y = 12\n\n⇒ (4x - 3y)² = 12²\n\n⇒ 16x2 + 9y2 - 24xy = 144\n\n⇒ 16x2 + 9y2 - 24 × 5 = 144\n\n⇒ 16x2 + 9y2 - 120 = 144\n\n⇒ 16x2 + 9y2 = 264\n\nNow,\n\nfrac{{16{x²} + 9{y²}}}{8} = frac{{264}}{8}\n\n⇒ 33\n\n**∴ The required answer is 33.**",
